<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The heart's good side (Source/ColonyCouncil/Heart/GoodHeart.cs), the player's request of 6 November 2026: the other
    side of strain. Its mood is situational like strain's: it reads the colonist's band of the good side each time the
    game asks and stores nothing in their memories. One stage a band, as the player approved them (6 November 2026):
    steady +2, in good heart +3, in high spirits +5 (HeartMath.GoodMood has the same); below steady, nothing yet, no
    mood. Words for every age.
  -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Heart_GoodSide</defName>
    <workerClass>ColonyCouncil.ThoughtWorker_HeartGood</workerClass>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_HeartGood</thoughtClass>
    <validWhileDespawned>true</validWhileDespawned>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>steady</label>
        <description>The days have been kind to me more often than not lately. I feel sure on my feet.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>2</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>in good heart</label>
        <description>The good days have been adding up: people I care about close by, and work that means something. It stays with me.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>3</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>in high spirits</label>
        <description>Everything has been going right for a good while now. I feel I could take on whatever comes.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>5</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <!--
    A kind word from someone in high spirits (the good side's release): they walked over and said it, face to face. A
    small good memory of Rimfolk's, so it comes as a small joy (a short moment, and what it weighs beyond eases the
    heart of whoever heard it).
  -->
  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>Council_Heart_KindWord</defName>
    <thoughtClass>ColonyCouncil.Thought_CouncilSocial</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>2</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>3</stackLimit>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>1</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>a kind word</label>
        <description>It was only a word or two, and it helped more than they know.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>3</baseMoodEffect>
        <baseOpinionOffset>6</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
